# scripts/rename/name.env — the ONE place the new name is spelled (U-W3.05, D9).
#
# scripts/rename/apply.sh sources this file (unless TARGET_NAME is already set
# in the environment, which wins) and derives every case form it needs from
# this single value. Nobody hand-types the target name into a mechanical
# surface: change it here, re-run apply.sh, done. Changing the target name
# after a bad reservation result (A3) is exactly this: edit this file, re-run.
#
# TARGET_NAME must be a single lowercase word: ^[a-z][a-z0-9]*$. apply.sh only
# knows how to derive lower/Title/UPPER forms for a single word (that is the
# scope this program needs -- "pix"). A multi-word target would need apply.sh's
# form derivation extended before this file's shape still works; that is a
# deliberate limitation, not an oversight.
TARGET_NAME="${TARGET_NAME:-pix}"
